---
config:
  flowchart:
    wrappingWidth: 400
---
flowchart TB
    accTitle: How the diagrams fix themselves
    accDescr: A pull request that adds a mermaid block or changes a diagram, and Renovate with a new version of mermaid-cli, run the check diagrams, which draws the diagrams anew. On a branch of the repository, the diagram bot commits the sources and pictures onto the branch, and the checks run again; a fork keeps the failing check, which says the command. After the merge, and every week, main is drawn too: when a diagram is not yet a picture of its source, one pull request from bot/diagrams fixes it and merges itself. So every reader sees every diagram.

    change["`A pull request adds a *mermaid* block<br>or changes a diagram`"]
    renovate["Renovate brings<br>a new mermaid-cli"]
    check{"The check diagrams:<br>every diagram a picture<br>of its source?"}
    bot["The diagram bot commits<br>sources and pictures<br>onto the branch"]
    fork["A fork: the check<br>says the command"]
    merged["The pull request merges"]
    main{"main, after every change<br>and every week:<br>every diagram a picture?"}
    fix["`One pull request from<br>*bot/diagrams* that<br>merges itself`"]
    done["Every reader sees<br>every diagram"]

    change --> check
    renovate --> check
    check -- "no, a branch" --> bot
    bot -- "checks again" --> check
    check -- "no, a fork" --> fork
    check -- "yes" --> merged --> main
    main -- "yes" --> done
    main -- "no" --> fix --> done

    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef person fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    class bot,renovate,fix bot
    class change,fork person
    class done done
